`742-749`: **🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration** | **<picture><img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/amber-16.svg" width="16" height="16" align="absmiddle" alt=""></picture> Minor** | **⚡ Quick win**

**Check the write result and write atomically.**

`QFile::open(WriteOnly)` truncates the existing file. The code then ignores the result of `f.write`. If the disk is full or an I/O error occurs, the caller's existing `.rtf` is destroyed and `saveRtf` still returns `true`. Session then reports a successful save.

<details>
<summary>🛡️ Proposed fix</summary>
<dl>
<dd>

```diff
-    QFile f(path);
-    if (!f.open(QIODevice::WriteOnly)) {
+    QSaveFile f(path);
+    if (!f.open(QIODevice::WriteOnly)) {
         if (error)
             *error = QStringLiteral("Cannot write ") + path;
         return false;
     }
-    f.write(rtf.toUtf8());
-    return true;
+    const QByteArray bytes = rtf.toUtf8();
+    if (f.write(bytes) != bytes.size() || !f.commit()) {
+        if (error)
+            *error = QStringLiteral("Cannot write ") + path;
+        return false;
+    }
+    return true;
```
</dd>
</dl>
</details>



